<H1 align=left><FONT size=4>Quick and Dirty Guide to Thurgadin Gate potion</FONT><FONT size=2><A name=1></A><BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Never be stuck again. Your porter may have been LD for the past hour, but you can get out of that dank dungeon with only a 10 second potion drinking time, for cheap.</FONT></H1>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>First step is to get your pottery skill up to par. The easiest and simplest way to achieve this is making Medium Bowls... simply combine..</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>a vendor bought Water Flask..<BR>a vendor bought Block of Clay..<BR>a vendor bought Medium Bowl Sketch..</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>onto a potters wheel. No need to fire it in a Kiln, just drop or destroy the finished product. In easily a half hour, and less than 100pp, you`ll reach the trivial for Medium Bowls at 122 skill. 122 Skill is plenty to go ahead with making Thurg Gate potions.</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>On a potters wheel, combine</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>3 Crystalline Silk`s (From crystal spiders in Crystal Caverns, stackable, very common)<BR>1 Small Brick of Velium (non-stackable, from orcs in Crystal Caverns, semi-rare to common)<BR>2 Glass Shards (stackable, can be purchased from the far left-most vendor in the Thurgadin bank)</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>results in an Unfired Vial.</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>..fire the Unfired Vial along with 1 High Quality Firing Sheet (also purchased from the far left-most vendor in the Thurg bank) in a Kiln.</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>results in Velium Vial (No Drop).</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>Now, the final step to make your potion...exit the bank, and take a right. About ten seconds down the hall towards the church(take a left at fork), go into the second building on the left..Frundle Frenkler is there behind the counter. You simply..</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>/say What Velium Vapors?</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>..and she`ll give you a four-slot container called Velium Purifier.</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>In this container, you combine..</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>your Velium Vial (No Drop)<BR>2 Small Pieces of Velium (stackable, drops from orcs in Crystal Caverns, semi-rare to common)</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>Abracadabra, the container disappears and you are holding the Vial of Velium Vapors (10 second cast of Thurgadin Gate, Lore, No Drop)<BR>---------------------------------------------------------<BR>To summarize...</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>In order to make one Thurg gate potion, you`re going to need the following...</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>3 Crystalline Silk`s (From crystal spiders in Crystal Caverns, stackable, very common)<BR>1 Small Brick of Velium (non-stackable, from orcs in Crystal Caverns, semi-rare to common)<BR>2 Glass Shards (stackable, can be purchased from the far left-most vendor in the Thurgadin bank)<BR>1 High Quality Firing Sheet (stackable, can be purchased from the far left-most vendor in the Thurgadin bank)<BR>2 Small Pieces of Velium (stackable, drops from orcs in Crystal Caverns, semi-rare to common)</FONT></P>
<P align=left></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>Since the final potion is Lore...you can`t have more than one at a time. There is a way to ensure you can easily make another Gate potion after you use one, however. Simply make as many Velium Vials as you would like, and keep them in the bank, along with 2 Small Pieces of Velium for every Velium Vial you have. <BR>Whenever you gate to Thurgadin, run over to Frundle, get a container, go to the bank and make the combine with the components you have all ready to go. A new Gate potion in about a minute and a half.</FONT></P>
<P align=left><FONT size=2>Since Thurgadin is only about a two minute run from the Plane of Knowledge book in Greater Divide, this potion is truly useful in getting around the world of Norrath.</FONT></P>
<P align=left>Good luck in your adventures.</P>
